failures: "3 guarded failure cases\nSee the recorded conditions and effects below" {
  link: "#process/interaction/publication"
  tooltip: "Admission, coherent inspection, freshness, candidate validation, or receipt preparation fails before a journal/authoritative replacement.\nReturn the applicable rejected, conflict, busy, or recovery-required result; do not publish the candidate.\nAuthoritative records are not changed by this failed attempt before publication. After non-preview exclusion begins, private directories, epoch, or lock cleanup effects may already exist.; Unavailable or malformed state is not converted into an empty current snapshot or a successful no-op.\n\nA non-crash failure occurs after the prepared journal is created but before committed phase.\nThe source attempts guarded restoration of exact before bytes and cleanup. If that succeeds, report the original failure; otherwise require explicit recovery.\nRestoration checks every current target against retained before/candidate identities and removes only tracked transaction-created files or empty created directories where permitted.; Observed unknown target bytes, missing/tampered evidence, or failed restoration prevent guessed repair; recovery metadata is reported only when available.\n\nExecution is interrupted, commitment/cleanup is uncertain, or a failure occurs with a committed journal.\nReport recovery-required when control returns with transaction attention, or leave the interrupted caller without a success receipt. Do not claim rollback or saved content from an unknown outcome.\nReaders do not expose an unfinished mixed store as current. Exact retained state and explicit recovery selection govern subsequent work.; A lost stdout response after successful commitment is a transport/lost-response problem. Retrying the old expected revision does not authorize replay; reread and reassess."
  style.fill: "#F9EEEE"
  style.stroke: "#597390"
  style.font-color: "#24364A"
  style.font-size: 16
  style.border-radius: 7
  style.stroke-dash: 3
}
